# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fourthwall — merch catalogue + checkout
#
# Both are optional. With neither set the shop renders from the local
# price table in src/lib/merch.ts and the checkout button explains that
# the shop is not open yet, which is the correct pre-launch state.
#
# Neither is NEXT_PUBLIC_: the catalogue is fetched server-side so it can
# use Next's fetch cache, and the cart is created in a server action.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Storefront token — Fourthwall admin › Settings › For developers.
# Public by design (prefix `ptkn_`), read-only over the catalogue.
FOURTHWALL_STOREFRONT_TOKEN=

# Host only, no scheme and no trailing slash. This is the custom checkout
# domain configured in the Fourthwall admin, e.g. shop.notiva.de — without
# one the customer visibly lands on *.fourthwall.com at the moment of
# payment.
FOURTHWALL_CHECKOUT_DOMAIN=

# After setting both, map the eight Notiva slugs to the product slugs in
# the shop: FOURTHWALL_SLUGS in src/lib/fourthwall/catalogue.ts.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe — donations only
#
# Merch is Fourthwall's; Stripe never touches it. Unset, the donate
# section reports that donations are not open yet.
#
# Notiva is NOT a charity: these are gifts to a for-profit company, not
# tax-deductible, and no receipt is issued.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dashboard › Developers › API keys. Use the test pair (sk_test_ /
# pk_test_) until the entity and bank account exist.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Required ONLY for the monthly supporter tiers. A subscription price
# must belong to a Product, so create one ("Notiva Unterstützung",
# recurring) and paste its prod_… id. The monthly amounts are priced
# against it at request time, which is what lets someone type their own
# figure instead of picking €5/€15/€50. Leave blank and the monthly path
# reports itself as not open; one-off donations still work.
STRIPE_DONATION_PRODUCT_ID=

# Dashboard › Developers › Webhooks, endpoint /api/webhooks/stripe.
# Subscribe to: payment_intent.succeeded, invoice.paid,
# invoice.payment_failed, customer.subscription.deleted.
# Locally: stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3001/api/webhooks/stripe
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lead capture — waitlist + investor deck requests
#
# POST /api/waitlist, GET /api/waitlist/confirm and POST /api/investor-deck
# write to public.waitlist_signup / public.investor_lead. Apply
# supabase/migrations/20260731120000_lead_capture.sql before first use.
#
# No new secrets are required: the routes connect over the DATABASE_URL that
# is already set for this app, and mail goes through the existing Resend key.
# Both must be present in the Amplify environment or the endpoints return
# 503 rather than accepting a submission they cannot keep.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase Postgres, Supavisor transaction pooler on :6543. Already set in
# .env / .env.production. src/lib/db.ts strips the Prisma-only query params
# (?schema, pgbouncer, connection_limit, pool_timeout) before connecting,
# because postgres.js would otherwise forward them as server startup
# parameters and the connection is rejected.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Required. Without it no confirmation mail can be sent, so POST /api/waitlist
# returns 502 rather than stranding a signup that can never be confirmed.
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Where deck requests and confirmed signups are announced, and the Reply-To on
# investor mail so answers do not vanish into the no-reply mailbox.
# Defaults to hikmat.imanov@notiva.de.
FOUNDER_EMAIL=

# Used to build the confirmation link, so it must be the public origin —
# a wrong value here produces confirmation emails nobody can complete.
# Already set to https://notiva.de.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_URL=
